English
────────────────────────────────────────

The code, web design, layout, text, icons and documentation in this repository and of the
"風電風情 · Taiwan Wind Watch" website, together with the data files and notes compiled,
checked and written by the lab (together, "the Work"), are copyrighted. All rights reserved.

1. What you may do
  a. View the website in a web browser and view the contents of this repository on GitHub.
  b. View and fork the repository within GitHub as GitHub's Terms of Service allow; a fork
     grants none of the rights listed under 2.
  c. Quote the Work within the limits of fair use under copyright law, crediting
     "National Chin-Yi University of Technology, Dept. Intelligent Automation Engineering,
     Dof Lab by Juihung Liu" and the URL.

2. What you may not do without written permission
  a. Copy, redistribute, republish or mirror all or part of the Work (including the
     single-file HTML copies).
  b. Modify, adapt or translate the Work, or create derivative works based on it.
  c. Deploy the Work or any part of it on another website, server or application.
  d. Use the Work or any part of it for any commercial purpose.

3. Third-party data and libraries
  Third-party data and libraries used by the Work remain under their original licences
  (listed in the README under "Data sources & license"); this licence does not restrict
  any right anyone has under those terms. In particular:
  - `data/global/turbines_osm.json` comes from OpenStreetMap and is shared under the
    Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 (© OpenStreetMap contributors); the restrictions of
    this licence do not apply to it.
  - Source data from government open data, CC BY 4.0, public-domain and similar sources are
    used under their own licences.
  - three.js (MIT) and Leaflet (BSD-2-Clause) are under their own licences.
  - Farm photos come from Wikimedia Commons; each photo's author and licence are shown with it.

4. Asking for permission
  To ask for any permission listed under 2 (for example teaching, research collaboration or
  republishing), please open an issue at https://github.com/dofliu/windfarmTaiwan/issues.

The Work is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied; the data are
not fully accurate, as the README explains.
